    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d508">

                <pb facs="0462" n="388" sameAs="frus:frus1865p2/pg388"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr. Pike</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 219.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-04-04"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >April</hi> 4, 1865.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Your despatch of the 15th of March, No.
                    157, has been received. The reaction of European opinion in regard to the United
                    States, which you have announced as having begun with the success of Major
                    General Sherman’s campaign, will doubtlessly be accelerated by the intelligence
                    which I have now the pleasure to communicate, that Petersburg and Richmond this
                    morning yielded before the advance of Lieutenant General Grant.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">James</hi> S. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Pike,</hi> Esq., <hi rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c.,
                        &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
